    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47A(4) Appeals from courts of summary jurisdiction",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-47a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Supreme Court of each State is invested with federal\njurisdiction, and jurisdiction is conferred on the Supreme Court of\neach Territory, with respect to matters arising under this Act, in\nrespect of which appeals are instituted under this section.\nNote:\nFor jurisdiction in relation to child support legislation, see section 101\nof the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 and section 106 of the\nChild Support (Registration and Collection) Act 1988.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Supreme Court of each State is invested with federal\njurisdiction, and jurisdiction is conferred on the Supreme Court of\neach Territory, with respect to matters arising under this Act, in\nrespect of which appeals are instituted under this section.\nNote:\nFor jurisdiction in relation to child support legislation, see section 101\nof the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 and section 106 of the\nChild Support (Registration and Collection) Act 1988.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "73fa81f8dd29156a4fe4eda78e6e8f08efa16c90f95a2f9712c115f5e18ab75f",
      "skos:note": "Supreme Court has federal jurisdiction over matters arising under the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-47a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47A(4) Appeals from courts of summary jurisdiction",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Supreme Court of each State is invested with federal\njurisdiction, and jurisdiction is conferred on the Supreme Court of\neach Territory, with respect to matters arising under this Act, in\nrespect of which appeals are instituted under this section.\nNote:\nFor jurisdiction in relation to child support legislation, see section 101\nof the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 and section 106 of the\nChild Support (Registration and Collection) Act 1988."
    },
