      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Governor-General may, by Proclamation, fix a date as the date\non or after which appeals to the Supreme Court of a specified State\nor Territory under this section may not be instituted, and such a\nProclamation may be expressed to apply only to proceedings of a\nspecified class or specified classes."
    },
