      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The court hearing an appeal under this section:\n(a) must proceed by way of a hearing de novo, but may receive\nas evidence any record of evidence given, including any\naffidavit filed or exhibit received, in the court of summary\njurisdiction; and\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The court hearing an appeal under this section:\n(a) must proceed by way of a hearing de novo, but may receive\nas evidence any record of evidence given, including any\naffidavit filed or exhibit received, in the court of summary\njurisdiction; and\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80db1766a85767e70fb625680cfde364444055cc04d1d4764bfcc44cff3e04d3",
      "skos:note": "Court must proceed by way of a hearing de novo."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-47a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47A(6) Appeals from courts of summary jurisdiction",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The court hearing an appeal under this section:\n(a) must proceed by way of a hearing de novo, but may receive\nas evidence any record of evidence given, including any\naffidavit filed or exhibit received, in the court of summary\njurisdiction; and\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia"
    },
