    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-70",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70 Subsection 55(5) (paragraphs (d) and (e) of the definition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-70"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "of appeal)\nRepeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n(d) a review by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) of the making, by the Chief Executive Officer,\nor a Senior Registrar or Registrar of that Court, of:\n(i) the divorce order; or\n(ii) an order under section 55A in relation to the\nproceedings in which the divorce order was made; or\n(iii) an order determining an application under section 57 or\n58 for rescission of the divorce order; or\n(e) a review by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) of the making, by the Chief Executive Officer,\nor a Senior Registrar or Registrar of that Court, of:\n(i) the divorce order; or\n(ii) an order under section 55A in relation to the\nproceedings in which the divorce order was made; or\n(iii) an order determining an application under section 57 or\n58 for rescission of the divorce order; or",
      "skos:definition": "of appeal)\nRepeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n(d) a review by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) of the making, by the Chief Executive Officer,\nor a Senior Registrar or Registrar of that Court, of:\n(i) the divorce order; or\n(ii) an order under section 55A in relation to the\nproceedings in which the divorce order was made; or\n(iii) an order determining an application under section 57 or\n58 for rescission of the divorce order; or\n(e) a review by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) of the making, by the Chief Executive Officer,\nor a Senior Registrar or Registrar of that Court, of:\n(i) the divorce order; or\n(ii) an order under section 55A in relation to the\nproceedings in which the divorce order was made; or\n(iii) an order determining an application under section 57 or\n58 for rescission of the divorce order; or",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-70-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-70-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "289c0aa1671e32e227f7a52c70366d682e4249e7ef3070a22107b5ccdb2a63c0",
      "skos:note": "Repeal of certain orders made by the Chief Executive Officer or a Senior Registrar/Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-70",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70 Subsection 55(5) (paragraphs (d) and (e) of the definition",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "of appeal)\nRepeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n(d) a review by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) of the making, by the Chief Executive Officer,\nor a Senior Registrar or Registrar of that Court, of:\n(i) the divorce order; or\n(ii) an order under section 55A in relation to the\nproceedings in which the divorce order was made; or\n(iii) an order determining an application under section 57 or\n58 for rescission of the divorce order; or\n(e) a review by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) of the making, by the Chief Executive Officer,\nor a Senior Registrar or Registrar of that Court, of:\n(i) the divorce order; or\n(ii) an order under section 55A in relation to the\nproceedings in which the divorce order was made; or\n(iii) an order determining an application under section 57 or\n58 for rescission of the divorce order; or"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-70-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-70"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
