    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18pa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18PA Marshal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-18pa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Marshal of the Court is responsible for:\n(a) the security of the Court; and\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(b) the personal security of the Judges and officers and staff of\nthe Court.\n(2) The Marshal of the Court is also responsible for:\n(a) taking, receiving and detaining all persons committed to the\nMarshal’s custody by the Court; and\n(b) discharging such persons when so directed by the Court or\notherwise required by law.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Marshal of the Court is responsible for:\n(a) the security of the Court; and\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(b) the personal security of the Judges and officers and staff of\nthe Court.\n(2) The Marshal of the Court is also responsible for:\n(a) taking, receiving and detaining all persons committed to the\nMarshal’s custody by the Court; and\n(b) discharging such persons when so directed by the Court or\notherwise required by law.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18pa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18pa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e44b23c341a06bd13c64eac69d265b2e7cc22a6d5b8e1765b4911c7607a227d9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-18pa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18PA Marshal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Marshal of the Court is responsible for:\n(a) the security of the Court; and\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(b) the personal security of the Judges and officers and staff of\nthe Court.\n(2) The Marshal of the Court is also responsible for:\n(a) taking, receiving and detaining all persons committed to the\nMarshal’s custody by the Court; and\n(b) discharging such persons when so directed by the Court or\notherwise required by law."
    },
    {
