      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n(2) Before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome\nfor the listed entity, if the outcome amount relates to the\nadministrative affairs of a court mentioned in an item of the\nfollowing table, the Chief Executive Officer must:\n(a) consult the person or persons mentioned in that item about\nthe spending; and\n(b) obtain the consent of:\n(i) the person or persons mentioned in that item to the\nspending; or\n(ii) the Attorney-General to the spending.\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nConsultation about spending\nItem\nCourt\nPersons to be consulted\nThe Court\nThe Chief Justice\nThe Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1)\nBoth:\n(a) the Chief Justice of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Court\nThe Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2)\nBoth:\n(a) the Chief Judge of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Court",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n(2) Before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome\nfor the listed entity, if the outcome amount relates to the\nadministrative affairs of a court mentioned in an item of the\nfollowing table, the Chief Executive Officer must:\n(a) consult the person or persons mentioned in that item about\nthe spending; and\n(b) obtain the consent of:\n(i) the person or persons mentioned in that item to the\nspending; or\n(ii) the Attorney-General to the spending.\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nConsultation about spending\nItem\nCourt\nPersons to be consulted\nThe Court\nThe Chief Justice\nThe Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1)\nBoth:\n(a) the Chief Justice of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Court\nThe Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2)\nBoth:\n(a) the Chief Judge of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Court",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-201-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-201-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed5785e2726446f0f6d63516e08fb4e17a6918bf0aae13845405fdc47419033b",
      "skos:note": "Consultation about spending before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-201",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "201 Subsections 18ZD(2) and (3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n(2) Before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome\nfor the listed entity, if the outcome amount relates to the\nadministrative affairs of a court mentioned in an item of the\nfollowing table, the Chief Executive Officer must:\n(a) consult the person or persons mentioned in that item about\nthe spending; and\n(b) obtain the consent of:\n(i) the person or persons mentioned in that item to the\nspending; or\n(ii) the Attorney-General to the spending.\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nConsultation about spending\nItem\nCourt\nPersons to be consulted\nThe Court\nThe Chief Justice\nThe Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1)\nBoth:\n(a) the Chief Justice of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Court\nThe Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2)\nBoth:\n(a) the Chief Judge of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Court"
    },
    {
