    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18zf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18ZF Making arrangements relating to APS employees",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-18zf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chief Executive Officer must make the services of APS\nemployees who are officers of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1), or staff of the Registries of the\nCourt, available for the purposes of assisting the Chief Executive\nOfficer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia in the\nperformance of functions under sections 84 and 278 of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Chief Executive Officer must make the services of APS\nemployees who are officers of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1), or staff of the Registries of the\nCourt, available for the purposes of assisting the Chief Executive\nOfficer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia in the\nperformance of functions under sections 84 and 278 of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18zf-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18zf-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a9bf292a0f7c466e32bd0e3189dab489723b876de00dc7826d2023eec185741",
      "skos:note": "Must make APS employees available for assisting the Chief Executive Officer in performing functions under sections 84 and 278 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-18zf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18ZF Making arrangements relating to APS employees",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chief Executive Officer must make the services of APS\nemployees who are officers of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1), or staff of the Registries of the\nCourt, available for the purposes of assisting the Chief Executive\nOfficer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia in the\nperformance of functions under sections 84 and 278 of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18zf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-18zf"
