      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32AD Confirmation of civil proceedings transferred from the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-32ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2)\n(1) If the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmakes an order under subsection 153(1) of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia Act 2021 transferring a proceeding to the\nCourt, the Court may, by order, confirm the transfer of the\nproceeding to the Court.\nNote:\nThe transfer of a proceeding takes effect on the day the Court makes\nan order under this section in relation to the proceeding: see\nsubsection 153(4) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.\n(2) The Court may, in its discretion, receive further evidence to decide\nwhether to make an order under subsection (1). Such evidence may\nbe taken in any of the ways mentioned in section 27.\n(3) The Court has jurisdiction in a matter that:\n(a) is the subject of a proceeding transferred to the Court by the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2);\nand\n(b) is a matter in which the Court does not have jurisdiction apart\nfrom this subsection.\nTo avoid doubt, the Court’s jurisdiction under this subsection is not\nsubject to limits set by another provision.\n(4) An appeal does not lie from a decision of the Court in relation to an\norder made under subsection (1) confirming the transfer of a\nproceeding.",
      "skos:definition": "Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2)\n(1) If the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmakes an order under subsection 153(1) of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia Act 2021 transferring a proceeding to the\nCourt, the Court may, by order, confirm the transfer of the\nproceeding to the Court.\nNote:\nThe transfer of a proceeding takes effect on the day the Court makes\nan order under this section in relation to the proceeding: see\nsubsection 153(4) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.\n(2) The Court may, in its discretion, receive further evidence to decide\nwhether to make an order under subsection (1). Such evidence may\nbe taken in any of the ways mentioned in section 27.\n(3) The Court has jurisdiction in a matter that:\n(a) is the subject of a proceeding transferred to the Court by the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2);\nand\n(b) is a matter in which the Court does not have jurisdiction apart\nfrom this subsection.\nTo avoid doubt, the Court’s jurisdiction under this subsection is not\nsubject to limits set by another provision.\n(4) An appeal does not lie from a decision of the Court in relation to an\norder made under subsection (1) confirming the transfer of a\nproceeding.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be3f12ae8034a4917ddc6c217cf6d40f10818652f1cb38fa3ce905294b4b276f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-32ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32AD Confirmation of civil proceedings transferred from the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2)\n(1) If the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmakes an order under subsection 153(1) of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia Act 2021 transferring a proceeding to the\nCourt, the Court may, by order, confirm the transfer of the\nproceeding to the Court.\nNote:\nThe transfer of a proceeding takes effect on the day the Court makes\nan order under this section in relation to the proceeding: see\nsubsection 153(4) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.\n(2) The Court may, in its discretion, receive further evidence to decide\nwhether to make an order under subsection (1). Such evidence may\nbe taken in any of the ways mentioned in section 27.\n(3) The Court has jurisdiction in a matter that:\n(a) is the subject of a proceeding transferred to the Court by the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2);\nand\n(b) is a matter in which the Court does not have jurisdiction apart\nfrom this subsection.\nTo avoid doubt, the Court’s jurisdiction under this subsection is not\nsubject to limits set by another provision.\n(4) An appeal does not lie from a decision of the Court in relation to an\norder made under subsection (1) confirming the transfer of a\nproceeding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32AD(1) Confirmation of civil proceedings transferred from the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmakes an order under subsection 153(1) of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia Act 2021 transferring a proceeding to the\nCourt, the Court may, by order, confirm the transfer of the\nproceeding to the Court.\nNote:\nThe transfer of a proceeding takes effect on the day the Court makes\nan order under this section in relation to the proceeding: see\nsubsection 153(4) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmakes an order under subsection 153(1) of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia Act 2021 transferring a proceeding to the\nCourt, the Court may, by order, confirm the transfer of the\nproceeding to the Court.\nNote:\nThe transfer of a proceeding takes effect on the day the Court makes\nan order under this section in relation to the proceeding: see\nsubsection 153(4) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99b31f3a2acddfdfe8243fe0b940bbc802d06fb603b6c1d5ab8f350afedbe1ff",
      "skos:note": "The Court may confirm the transfer of a proceeding to itself."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32AD(1) Confirmation of civil proceedings transferred from the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmakes an order under subsection 153(1) of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia Act 2021 transferring a proceeding to the\nCourt, the Court may, by order, confirm the transfer of the\nproceeding to the Court.\nNote:\nThe transfer of a proceeding takes effect on the day the Court makes\nan order under this section in relation to the proceeding: see\nsubsection 153(4) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "May confirm transfer",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32AD(2) Confirmation of civil proceedings transferred from the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Court may, in its discretion, receive further evidence to decide\nwhether to make an order under subsection (1). Such evidence may\nbe taken in any of the ways mentioned in section 27.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Court may, in its discretion, receive further evidence to decide\nwhether to make an order under subsection (1). Such evidence may\nbe taken in any of the ways mentioned in section 27.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "079269a74d2f94f4c0d08a30a052cafd5064d4e689e41e64634da4f60e61eaf2",
      "skos:note": "Court may receive further evidence to decide on making an order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32AD(2) Confirmation of civil proceedings transferred from the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Court may, in its discretion, receive further evidence to decide\nwhether to make an order under subsection (1). Such evidence may\nbe taken in any of the ways mentioned in section 27."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ad-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
