    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-223",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "223 Subsection 49(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-223"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(2) If:\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(a) the Court reserves judgment in a proceeding; and\n(b) a Judge who heard the proceeding, whether as a single Judge\nor as a member of a Full Court, prepares orders and reasons;\nthose orders and reasons may be made public by another Judge on\nbehalf of the Judge who heard the proceeding or as otherwise\nprovided for by the Rules of Court.\n(2A) If:\n(a) the Court reserves reasons for its decision in a proceeding;\nand\n(b) a Judge who heard the proceeding, whether as a single Judge\nor as a member of a Full Court, prepares reasons;\nthose reasons may be made public by another Judge on behalf of\nthe Judge who heard the proceeding or as otherwise provided for\nby the Rules of Court.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(2) If:\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(a) the Court reserves judgment in a proceeding; and\n(b) a Judge who heard the proceeding, whether as a single Judge\nor as a member of a Full Court, prepares orders and reasons;\nthose orders and reasons may be made public by another Judge on\nbehalf of the Judge who heard the proceeding or as otherwise\nprovided for by the Rules of Court.\n(2A) If:\n(a) the Court reserves reasons for its decision in a proceeding;\nand\n(b) a Judge who heard the proceeding, whether as a single Judge\nor as a member of a Full Court, prepares reasons;\nthose reasons may be made public by another Judge on behalf of\nthe Judge who heard the proceeding or as otherwise provided for\nby the Rules of Court.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-223-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-223-ss-2a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-223",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "223 Subsection 49(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(2) If:\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(a) the Court reserves judgment in a proceeding; and\n(b) a Judge who heard the proceeding, whether as a single Judge\nor as a member of a Full Court, prepares orders and reasons;\nthose orders and reasons may be made public by another Judge on\nbehalf of the Judge who heard the proceeding or as otherwise\nprovided for by the Rules of Court.\n(2A) If:\n(a) the Court reserves reasons for its decision in a proceeding;\nand\n(b) a Judge who heard the proceeding, whether as a single Judge\nor as a member of a Full Court, prepares reasons;\nthose reasons may be made public by another Judge on behalf of\nthe Judge who heard the proceeding or as otherwise provided for\nby the Rules of Court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-223-ss-2",
