    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-236",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "236 Seals and stamps",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-236"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "Despite the amendment of paragraph 123(1)(f) of the Family Law Act\n1975 by this Schedule:\n(a) a seal of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of Court\nand in force immediately before the commencement day,\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nmay be affixed to documents (in accordance with\nsubsection 59(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period\nbeginning on the commencement day, as if it were a seal of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1); and\n(b) a stamp of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of\nCourt and in force immediately before the commencement\nday, may be affixed to documents (in accordance with\nsubsection 60(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period\nbeginning on the commencement day, as if it were a stamp of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1).",
      "skos:definition": "Despite the amendment of paragraph 123(1)(f) of the Family Law Act\n1975 by this Schedule:\n(a) a seal of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of Court\nand in force immediately before the commencement day,\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nmay be affixed to documents (in accordance with\nsubsection 59(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period\nbeginning on the commencement day, as if it were a seal of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1); and\n(b) a stamp of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of\nCourt and in force immediately before the commencement\nday, may be affixed to documents (in accordance with\nsubsection 60(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period\nbeginning on the commencement day, as if it were a stamp of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-236-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-236-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c68e4a29bd26fb6ba522856af4bd60af861022583384ad3867af33f1ab91722a",
      "skos:note": "Affixing seal or stamp of Family Court until end of 12-month period"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-236",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "236 Seals and stamps",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "Despite the amendment of paragraph 123(1)(f) of the Family Law Act\n1975 by this Schedule:\n(a) a seal of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of Court\nand in force immediately before the commencement day,\n\nAmendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nmay be affixed to documents (in accordance with\nsubsection 59(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period\nbeginning on the commencement day, as if it were a seal of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1); and\n(b) a stamp of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of\nCourt and in force immediately before the commencement\nday, may be affixed to documents (in accordance with\nsubsection 60(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period\nbeginning on the commencement day, as if it were a stamp of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-236-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-236"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-236-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to affix seal or stamp",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "237 Continuity of Rules of Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-237"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "The amendments made by items 130, 139, 152, 165 and 167 of this\nSchedule:\n(a) do not affect the continuity of any Rules of Court made for\nthe purposes of section 123 of the Family Law Act 1975 that\nare in force immediately before the commencement day; and\n(b) to avoid doubt, do not prevent the amendment or repeal of\nthose Rules of Court.",
      "skos:definition": "The amendments made by items 130, 139, 152, 165 and 167 of this\nSchedule:\n(a) do not affect the continuity of any Rules of Court made for\nthe purposes of section 123 of the Family Law Act 1975 that\nare in force immediately before the commencement day; and\n(b) to avoid doubt, do not prevent the amendment or repeal of\nthose Rules of Court.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a22dd1032457caf094a3ed855bf67911fd8e1edb0484a966680bc5546d33c7c",
      "skos:note": "Amendments do not affect continuity of certain Rules of Court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-237",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "237 Continuity of Rules of Court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "The amendments made by items 130, 139, 152, 165 and 167 of this\nSchedule:\n(a) do not affect the continuity of any Rules of Court made for\nthe purposes of section 123 of the Family Law Act 1975 that\nare in force immediately before the commencement day; and\n(b) to avoid doubt, do not prevent the amendment or repeal of\nthose Rules of Court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-238",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "238 Registries of the Federal Court of Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-238"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia\nAct 1976 by this Schedule, a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia,\nexisting immediately before the commencement day, continues in\nexistence on and after that day.\n(2)\nThe amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act\n1976 by this Schedule does not affect:\n(a) the designation, before the commencement day, of a Registry\nof the Federal Court of Australia as the Principal Registry of\nthe Court; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nDespite the amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia\nAct 1976 by this Schedule, a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia,\nexisting immediately before the commencement day, continues in\nexistence on and after that day.\n(2)\nThe amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act\n1976 by this Schedule does not affect:\n(a) the designation, before the commencement day, of a Registry\nof the Federal Court of Australia as the Principal Registry of\nthe Court; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-238-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1a28c9a400f327c48c354a45ca0aa520a44eb95d925fe9c5d27eee39e7bffe6",
      "skos:note": "Continuation of existing Registry on commencement day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-1-sec-238",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "238 Registries of the Federal Court of Australia",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia\nAct 1976 by this Schedule, a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia,\nexisting immediately before the commencement day, continues in\nexistence on and after that day.\n(2)\nThe amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act\n1976 by this Schedule does not affect:\n(a) the designation, before the commencement day, of a Registry\nof the Federal Court of Australia as the Principal Registry of\nthe Court; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia"
    },
    {
