      "skos:note": "Supreme Court of the Northern Territory has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a decree of a court of summary jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-2-sec-106-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "106(2) Appeals from courts of summary jurisdiction",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Supreme Court of the Northern Territory has jurisdiction to\nhear and determine appeals from a decree of a court of summary\njurisdiction of the Northern Territory.\nNote:\nSee sections 47A and 47B of the Family Law Act 1975."
    },
