      "values:originalText": "This Part is about the jurisdiction and powers of the courts in\nrelation to matters arising under this Act.\nDivisions 2 and 3 confer jurisdiction on the Federal Court and the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2). That\njurisdiction is generally required to be exercised in the Fair Work\nDivisions of those courts.\nDivision 4 deals with intervention, costs, limitation on\nimprisonment, and regulations, in relation to proceedings in the\nFederal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) and, in some cases, a court of a State or Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "This Part is about the jurisdiction and powers of the courts in\nrelation to matters arising under this Act.\nDivisions 2 and 3 confer jurisdiction on the Federal Court and the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2). That\njurisdiction is generally required to be exercised in the Fair Work\nDivisions of those courts.\nDivision 4 deals with intervention, costs, limitation on\nimprisonment, and regulations, in relation to proceedings in the\nFederal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) and, in some cases, a court of a State or Territory.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-560-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-560-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56ccd0df8455b3062a0243373bb30476b7babe3fb0cddb0208a5d2be348fdad9",
      "skos:note": "Jurisdiction of Federal Court and Family Court of Australia"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-2-sec-560",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "560 Guide to this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "This Part is about the jurisdiction and powers of the courts in\nrelation to matters arising under this Act.\nDivisions 2 and 3 confer jurisdiction on the Federal Court and the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2). That\njurisdiction is generally required to be exercised in the Fair Work\nDivisions of those courts.\nDivision 4 deals with intervention, costs, limitation on\nimprisonment, and regulations, in relation to proceedings in the\nFederal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) and, in some cases, a court of a State or Territory."
    },
