          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-676-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "512fd7439771398c7c326c1a8bc4950222dc7f0c1218b33320fecf89ea0051e5",
      "skos:note": "Appeals with respect to PPS matters do not lie from certain courts."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-2-sec-676",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "676 Section 208 (table)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the table, substitute:\n\nFurther consequential amendments  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nCross-jurisdictional appeals\nItem\nUnless expressly provided by a law\nof the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, an appeal with respect to\na PPS matter does not lie from a\ndecision of ...\nto any of the following courts:\nthe Federal Court\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1);\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(c) a court of a State;\n(d) a court of a Territory.\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 1)\n(a) the Federal Court;\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(c) a court of a State;\n(d) a court of a Territory.\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 2)\n(a) a court of a State;\n(b) a court of a Territory.\na court of a State (other than a State\nFamily Court)\n(a) the Federal Court;\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1);\n(c) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(d) a court of another State;\n(e) a court of a Territory;\n(f) a State Family Court of the same\nState.\na court of the Australian Capital\nTerritory\n(a) the Federal Court;\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1);\n(c) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(d) a court of a State;\n(e) a court of another Territory.\na court of the Northern Territory\n(a) the Federal Court;\n\nSchedule 2  Further consequential amendments\n\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\nNo. 13, 2021\nCross-jurisdictional appeals\nItem\nUnless expressly provided by a law\nof the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, an appeal with respect to\na PPS matter does not lie from a\ndecision of ...\nto any of the following courts:\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1);\n(c) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(d) a court of a State;\n(e) a court of another Territory.\na court of an external Territory\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1);\n(b) Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(c) a court of a State;\n(d) a court of another Territory\n(whether internal or external).\na State Family Court\n(a) the Federal Court;\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2);\n(c) the Supreme Court of the same\nState;\n(d) a court of another State;\n(e) a court of a Territory."
    },
