      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.179",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(5) Subsection (4) does not limit the power of the Chief Judge of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) to make\nRules of Court under Chapter 4 of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia Act 2021 that are consistent with the regulations\nreferred to in that subsection.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(5) Subsection (4) does not limit the power of the Chief Judge of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) to make\nRules of Court under Chapter 4 of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia Act 2021 that are consistent with the regulations\nreferred to in that subsection.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-693-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ca62569ca6568a507050b56254c3d23a976e9c75f1c776b0e5cd356bdea2de63",
      "skos:note": "Repeal subsection, substitute with new provision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-2-sec-693",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "693 Subsection 56A(5)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 179,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(5) Subsection (4) does not limit the power of the Chief Judge of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) to make\nRules of Court under Chapter 4 of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia Act 2021 that are consistent with the regulations\nreferred to in that subsection."
    },
