        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Seals and stamps",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-3-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.200",
      "values:originalText": "Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999:\n(a) the seal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, existing\nimmediately before the commencement day, may be affixed\nto documents (in accordance with subsection 178(3) of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021)\nuntil the end of the 12-month period beginning on the\ncommencement day, as if it were the seal of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); and\n(b) a Federal Circuit Court of Australia stamp, existing\nimmediately before the commencement day, may be affixed\nto documents (in accordance with subsection 179(3) of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021)\nuntil the end of the 12-month period beginning on the\ncommencement day, as if it were a stamp of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2).",
      "skos:definition": "Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999:\n(a) the seal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, existing\nimmediately before the commencement day, may be affixed\nto documents (in accordance with subsection 178(3) of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021)\nuntil the end of the 12-month period beginning on the\ncommencement day, as if it were the seal of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); and\n(b) a Federal Circuit Court of Australia stamp, existing\nimmediately before the commencement day, may be affixed\nto documents (in accordance with subsection 179(3) of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021)\nuntil the end of the 12-month period beginning on the\ncommencement day, as if it were a stamp of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-5-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a6b172b54e204b2dc0043adc9788fe0e3496edd6cdd1134303e7231e8aa0eea",
      "skos:note": "Seal and stamp provisions for Federal Circuit Court of Australia"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-3-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Seals and stamps",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 200,
      "values:originalText": "Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999:\n(a) the seal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, existing\nimmediately before the commencement day, may be affixed\nto documents (in accordance with subsection 178(3) of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021)\nuntil the end of the 12-month period beginning on the\ncommencement day, as if it were the seal of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); and\n(b) a Federal Circuit Court of Australia stamp, existing\nimmediately before the commencement day, may be affixed\nto documents (in accordance with subsection 179(3) of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021)\nuntil the end of the 12-month period beginning on the\ncommencement day, as if it were a stamp of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)."
    },
    {
