      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Certification of retired disabled Judges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-3-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.201",
      "values:originalText": "A certification by the Minister under paragraph 9A(2)(a) of Schedule 1\nto the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999 before the\ncommencement day that a person is a retired disabled Judge has effect,\non and after that day, as if it were a certification by the Minister under\nsection 122 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021 that the person is a retired disabled Judge.",
      "skos:definition": "A certification by the Minister under paragraph 9A(2)(a) of Schedule 1\nto the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999 before the\ncommencement day that a person is a retired disabled Judge has effect,\non and after that day, as if it were a certification by the Minister under\nsection 122 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021 that the person is a retired disabled Judge.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-11-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb8e1b8abd2f30a5b0537a6bc0da34d2083eb01a5d5e18394070634bb26a98b3",
      "skos:note": "Certification of retired disabled Judges"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-3-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Certification of retired disabled Judges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 201,
      "values:originalText": "A certification by the Minister under paragraph 9A(2)(a) of Schedule 1\nto the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999 before the\ncommencement day that a person is a retired disabled Judge has effect,\non and after that day, as if it were a certification by the Minister under\nsection 122 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021 that the person is a retired disabled Judge."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-11-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-11"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Right of appeal to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-3-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.201",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999,\napplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of:\n(a) a refusal, before the commencement day, of the Minister to\ncertify that a Judge is a retired disabled Judge under\nsubclause 9A(2) of Schedule 1 to that Act; or\n(b) a refusal, before the commencement day, by the Minister\nunder paragraph 9D(9)(b) of Schedule 1 to that Act to give a\ndirection;\nif, on the commencement day, the time for making an application for\nreview of the refusal has not ended.\n(2)\nDespite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999,\napplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of any of the following decisions:\n\nSchedule 3  Repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nDespite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999,\napplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of:\n(a) a refusal, before the commencement day, of the Minister to\ncertify that a Judge is a retired disabled Judge under\nsubclause 9A(2) of Schedule 1 to that Act; or\n(b) a refusal, before the commencement day, by the Minister\nunder paragraph 9D(9)(b) of Schedule 1 to that Act to give a\ndirection;\nif, on the commencement day, the time for making an application for\nreview of the refusal has not ended.\n(2)\nDespite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999,\napplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of any of the following decisions:\n\nSchedule 3  Repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10106d8f253f7fccb2bdc0ae3469d98a274af1097f55cfb929e51dab6d192ac1",
      "skos:note": "Right of appeal to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-3-sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Right of appeal to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 201,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999,\napplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of:\n(a) a refusal, before the commencement day, of the Minister to\ncertify that a Judge is a retired disabled Judge under\nsubclause 9A(2) of Schedule 1 to that Act; or\n(b) a refusal, before the commencement day, by the Minister\nunder paragraph 9D(9)(b) of Schedule 1 to that Act to give a\ndirection;\nif, on the commencement day, the time for making an application for\nreview of the refusal has not ended.\n(2)\nDespite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999,\napplications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of any of the following decisions:\n\nSchedule 3  Repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12-logic-deontic-1",
