      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.206",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Court of Appeal established under the Supreme Court Act\n1935 (WA) and the Family Court of Western Australia are each\ninvested with federal jurisdiction with respect to matters arising\nunder Part VIIIC of this Act in respect of which appeals are\ninstituted under this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Court of Appeal established under the Supreme Court Act\n1935 (WA) and the Family Court of Western Australia are each\ninvested with federal jurisdiction with respect to matters arising\nunder Part VIIIC of this Act in respect of which appeals are\ninstituted under this section.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-4-sec-47ba"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-4-sec-47ba-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-4-sec-47ba-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e2acd01e0efd9b48ecc5b22602a0a8288794c3ee822b95f022a5bdcc1fcb020b",
      "skos:note": "Establishes federal jurisdiction for appeals under Part VIIIC."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-4-sec-47ba-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47BA(3) Appeals relating to matters arising under Part VIIIC",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 206,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Court of Appeal established under the Supreme Court Act\n1935 (WA) and the Family Court of Western Australia are each\ninvested with federal jurisdiction with respect to matters arising\nunder Part VIIIC of this Act in respect of which appeals are\ninstituted under this section."
    },
