      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.214",
      "values:originalText": "In this Schedule:\ncommencement day means the day this Schedule commences.\nFamily Court of a State means a court to which section 41 of the\nFamily Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act, applies.\nFamily Court of Australia means the federal court known, immediately\nbefore the commencement day, as the Family Court of Australia.\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia has the same meaning\nas in the new law.\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia means the federal court known,\nimmediately before the commencement day, as the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\nFederal Court means the Federal Court of Australia.\nFull Court, in relation to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1), means 2 or more Judges of the Court.\nnew law means the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court",
      "skos:definition": "In this Schedule:\ncommencement day means the day this Schedule commences.\nFamily Court of a State means a court to which section 41 of the\nFamily Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act, applies.\nFamily Court of Australia means the federal court known, immediately\nbefore the commencement day, as the Family Court of Australia.\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia has the same meaning\nas in the new law.\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia means the federal court known,\nimmediately before the commencement day, as the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\nFederal Court means the Federal Court of Australia.\nFull Court, in relation to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1), means 2 or more Judges of the Court.\nnew law means the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court",
      "cml:asserts": [
