      },
      "cml:premiseText": "new law means the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Continuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Change in title of judicial offices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.215",
      "values:originalText": "Chief Justice\n(1)\nThe office of Chief Justice of the Family Court of Australia under the\nold law is the same office as the office of Chief Justice of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the new law.\nDeputy Chief Justice\n(2)\nThe office of Deputy Chief Justice of the Family Court of Australia\nunder the old law is the same office as the office of Deputy Chief\nJustice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)\nunder the new law.\nSenior Judges\n(3)\nThe office of Senior Judge of the Family Court of Australia under the\nold law is the same office as the office of Senior Judge of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the new law.\nJudges\n(4)\nThe office of Judge (other than Senior Judge) of the Family Court of\nAustralia under the old law is the same office as the office of Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the\nnew law.\n(5)\nIn this item:\nold law means Part IV of the Family Law Act 1975, as in force\nimmediately before the commencement day.",
      "skos:definition": "Chief Justice\n(1)\nThe office of Chief Justice of the Family Court of Australia under the\nold law is the same office as the office of Chief Justice of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the new law.\nDeputy Chief Justice\n(2)\nThe office of Deputy Chief Justice of the Family Court of Australia\nunder the old law is the same office as the office of Deputy Chief\nJustice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)\nunder the new law.\nSenior Judges\n(3)\nThe office of Senior Judge of the Family Court of Australia under the\nold law is the same office as the office of Senior Judge of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the new law.\nJudges\n(4)\nThe office of Judge (other than Senior Judge) of the Family Court of\nAustralia under the old law is the same office as the office of Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the\nnew law.\n(5)\nIn this item:\nold law means Part IV of the Family Law Act 1975, as in force\nimmediately before the commencement day.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20b59d188b9c087611e76cf6ae966f499cd1cf337198ec6bf2d6580f2ed2fcb0",
      "skos:note": "Change in title of judicial offices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Change in title of judicial offices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 215,
      "values:originalText": "Chief Justice\n(1)\nThe office of Chief Justice of the Family Court of Australia under the\nold law is the same office as the office of Chief Justice of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the new law.\nDeputy Chief Justice\n(2)\nThe office of Deputy Chief Justice of the Family Court of Australia\nunder the old law is the same office as the office of Deputy Chief\nJustice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)\nunder the new law.\nSenior Judges\n(3)\nThe office of Senior Judge of the Family Court of Australia under the\nold law is the same office as the office of Senior Judge of the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the new law.\nJudges\n(4)\nThe office of Judge (other than Senior Judge) of the Family Court of\nAustralia under the old law is the same office as the office of Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) under the\nnew law.\n(5)\nIn this item:\nold law means Part IV of the Family Law Act 1975, as in force\nimmediately before the commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Same office under old and new law",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "old law means Part IV of the Family Law Act 1975, as in force immediately before the commencement day.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The office is the same under both laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Same class hierarchy for judicial offices",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:conclusionText": "The titles of judicial offices are part of a hierarchical structure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Appointments to judicial offices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
