    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Things done by the Family Court of Australia or Judges of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.217",
      "values:originalText": "the Court\nTo avoid doubt, the amendments made by this Act do not affect the\nvalidity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in\nrelation to:\n(a) the Family Court of Australia; or\n(b) a Full Court of the Family Court of Australia; or\n(c) the Chief Justice, the Deputy Chief Justice, a Senior Judge or\na Judge of the Family Court of Australia; or\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "the Court\nTo avoid doubt, the amendments made by this Act do not affect the\nvalidity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in\nrelation to:\n(a) the Family Court of Australia; or\n(b) a Full Court of the Family Court of Australia; or\n(c) the Chief Justice, the Deputy Chief Justice, a Senior Judge or\na Judge of the Family Court of Australia; or\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "739e3f8ab466747c69cb14a47ec2e716893b440fe3ff2da74ae8608a0a24d937",
      "skos:note": "Amendments do not affect validity of actions taken before commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Things done by the Family Court of Australia or Judges of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 217,
      "values:originalText": "the Court\nTo avoid doubt, the amendments made by this Act do not affect the\nvalidity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in\nrelation to:\n(a) the Family Court of Australia; or\n(b) a Full Court of the Family Court of Australia; or\n(c) the Chief Justice, the Deputy Chief Justice, a Senior Judge or\na Judge of the Family Court of Australia; or\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-7"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-7-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to maintain validity of actions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Actions taken before commencement day are valid.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Amendments do not affect validity of these actions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "Officer\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of\nthe Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes\nof the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief\nExecutive Officer of the Family Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Officer\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of\nthe Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes\nof the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief\nExecutive Officer of the Family Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-8-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ac7fd3628436d7a533fbf0b14f89edfc43a29ed3fcba30cbe53c669dbafc783",
      "skos:note": "Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia are taken to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 218,
      "values:originalText": "Officer\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of\nthe Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes\nof the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief\nExecutive Officer of the Family Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
