      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Things done by, or in relation to, a Registrar or Deputy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "Registrar\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court\nof Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of\nany law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or\nin relation to, a Senior Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of\nthe Family Court of Australia.\n(3)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Deputy Registrar of the\nFamily Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of\nthe operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1).\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court",
      "skos:definition": "Registrar\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court\nof Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of\nany law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or\nin relation to, a Senior Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of\nthe Family Court of Australia.\n(3)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Deputy Registrar of the\nFamily Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of\nthe operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1).\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9260d65bdba19f858cb7ef49de8d8c70242477956029eac3ea889f4432e7e16f",
      "skos:note": "Things done by, or in relation to, a Registrar or Deputy are taken to have been done by, or in relation to, a Senior Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Things done by, or in relation to, a Registrar or Deputy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 218,
      "values:originalText": "Registrar\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court\nof Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of\nany law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or\nin relation to, a Senior Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of\nthe Family Court of Australia.\n(3)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Deputy Registrar of the\nFamily Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of\nthe operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1).\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court"
    },
