    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Officers and staff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA person who, immediately before the commencement day, was an\nofficer of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as mentioned in\nparagraph 99(1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of the old law, continues on\nand after that day as an officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 2).\n(2)\nA person who, immediately before the commencement day, was a\nmember of the staff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia (as\nmentioned in section 112 of the old law), continues on and after that day\nas a member of the staff of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2).\n(3)\nIn this item:\nold law means the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, as in\nforce immediately before the commencement day.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nA person who, immediately before the commencement day, was an\nofficer of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as mentioned in\nparagraph 99(1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of the old law, continues on\nand after that day as an officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 2).\n(2)\nA person who, immediately before the commencement day, was a\nmember of the staff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia (as\nmentioned in section 112 of the old law), continues on and after that day\nas a member of the staff of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2).\n(3)\nIn this item:\nold law means the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, as in\nforce immediately before the commencement day.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-16-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e50431bab7340e9423f8e874b64cfa4e8828d4d11b772d46e9ac6950f181a0c7",
      "skos:note": "Continuation of officers and staff after commencement day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Officers and staff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA person who, immediately before the commencement day, was an\nofficer of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as mentioned in\nparagraph 99(1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of the old law, continues on\nand after that day as an officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court\nof Australia (Division 2).\n(2)\nA person who, immediately before the commencement day, was a\nmember of the staff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia (as\nmentioned in section 112 of the old law), continues on and after that day\nas a member of the staff of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2).\n(3)\nIn this item:\nold law means the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, as in\nforce immediately before the commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-16-norm",
