    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Application of subsection 25B(1) of the Acts Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "Act 1901\nSubsection 25B(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies as if:\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court of Australia were a body; and\n(b) the offices of Chief Judge and Judge were offices.",
      "skos:definition": "Act 1901\nSubsection 25B(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies as if:\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court of Australia were a body; and\n(b) the offices of Chief Judge and Judge were offices.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-17-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-17-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ebf737ed74cd8db9dbded927f38f55cec630b7a2eb65ce3ea5fd2808355966b5",
      "skos:note": "Act applies as if Federal Circuit Court of Australia were a body and offices of Chief Judge and Judge were offices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Application of subsection 25B(1) of the Acts Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "Act 1901\nSubsection 25B(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies as if:\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court of Australia were a body; and\n(b) the offices of Chief Judge and Judge were offices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-17-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-17"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-17-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "applies as if",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes obligation on the State to apply the provision",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Things done by, or in relation to, the Federal Circuit Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "of Australia or Judges of the Court\nTo avoid doubt, the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act\n1999, and any other amendment made by this Act, does not affect the\nvalidity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in\nrelation to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court of Australia; or\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the\nCourt  Part 3\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(b) the Chief Judge or a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia; or\n(c) a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia as a Federal\nMagistrate; or\n(d) a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia (including\nthe Chief Judge) when performing functions, or exercising\npowers, under an Act in the Judge’s personal capacity.\nNote:\nParagraph (d)—if a Judge may issue a warrant under an Act and does so, the Judge\nissues the warrant in the Judge’s personal capacity and not as a member of a court.",
      "skos:definition": "of Australia or Judges of the Court\nTo avoid doubt, the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act\n1999, and any other amendment made by this Act, does not affect the\nvalidity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in\nrelation to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court of Australia; or\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the\nCourt  Part 3\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(b) the Chief Judge or a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia; or\n(c) a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia as a Federal\nMagistrate; or\n(d) a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia (including\nthe Chief Judge) when performing functions, or exercising\npowers, under an Act in the Judge’s personal capacity.\nNote:\nParagraph (d)—if a Judge may issue a warrant under an Act and does so, the Judge\nissues the warrant in the Judge’s personal capacity and not as a member of a court.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-18-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-18-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64f85af84bbcff0c6dd58d7795f9f5d25c255eba0b511936882d42868d514f4c",
      "skos:note": "Validity of actions done before commencement day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Things done by, or in relation to, the Federal Circuit Court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "of Australia or Judges of the Court\nTo avoid doubt, the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act\n1999, and any other amendment made by this Act, does not affect the\nvalidity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in\nrelation to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court of Australia; or\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nContinuity of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the\nCourt  Part 3\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(b) the Chief Judge or a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia; or\n(c) a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia as a Federal\nMagistrate; or\n(d) a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia (including\nthe Chief Judge) when performing functions, or exercising\npowers, under an Act in the Judge’s personal capacity.\nNote:\nParagraph (d)—if a Judge may issue a warrant under an Act and does so, the Judge\nissues the warrant in the Judge’s personal capacity and not as a member of a court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-18-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-18"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-18-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Negative obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19 Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.223",
      "values:originalText": "Officer\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the\npurposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement\nday, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer\nof the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief\nExecutive Officer of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Officer\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the\npurposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement\nday, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer\nof the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief\nExecutive Officer of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-logic-deontic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e8f09ced04fdf28a6ad9bab2b5bb55f649ffb93baca96445fd2042277353784e",
      "skos:note": "Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer are taken as having been done by, or in relation to, the new entity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-19",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19 Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 223,
      "values:originalText": "Officer\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the\npurposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement\nday, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer\nof the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief\nExecutive Officer of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-19"
      },
