    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 Things done by, or in relation to, a Registrar",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.223",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the purposes\nof the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 2).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the purposes\nof the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 2).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-20-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-20-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-20-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d35e7cd13d038be9be305a9d2265b2d5785288305a84e625d7bd2aacf727d3cc",
      "skos:note": "Prescribes how things done by a Registrar are treated for the purposes of laws on and after commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 Things done by, or in relation to, a Registrar",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 223,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the purposes\nof the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have\nbeen done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 2).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions"
    },
