    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Things done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.224",
      "values:originalText": "Sheriff\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy Sheriff\nof the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the\npurposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement\nday, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy\nSheriff of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a\nDeputy Sheriff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Sheriff\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy Sheriff\nof the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the\npurposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement\nday, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy\nSheriff of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a\nDeputy Sheriff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-21-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ad5a18e2ad2a468aafd9ca92f1da3cd5dd1cefe14294cd3c3a9162a86d860e01",
      "skos:note": "Things done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy are taken as having been done by the new court authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Things done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 224,
      "values:originalText": "Sheriff\n(1)\nIf a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy Sheriff\nof the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, then, despite the repeal of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, the thing is taken, for the\npurposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement\nday, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a Deputy\nSheriff of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2).\n(2)\nThe Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply\nin relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Sheriff or a\nDeputy Sheriff of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument.\n(4)\nA determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
