        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "allows",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The provision allows the Minister to determine that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Marshal or a Deputy.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-22-logic-deontic-6",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "prohibits",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The provision prohibits making an instrument from being taken as having been done by, or in relation to, the Marshal or a Deputy.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-23",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23 Registries",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.225",
      "values:originalText": "Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, a\nRegistry of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, existing immediately\nbefore the commencement day, continues in existence on and after that\nday as a Registry of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2).",
      "skos:definition": "Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, a\nRegistry of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, existing immediately\nbefore the commencement day, continues in existence on and after that\nday as a Registry of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-23-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-23-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4cc87c6b34a19f5057efe7bf69e8ef397d26d91eb35ca3f5e604ea0cff388e48",
      "skos:note": "Registry continuation after repeal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-23",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23 Registries",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 225,
      "values:originalText": "Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, a\nRegistry of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, existing immediately\nbefore the commencement day, continues in existence on and after that\nday as a Registry of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-23-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-23"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-23-logic-alleninterval-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval application",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "commencement day",
      "cml:conclusionText": "on and after that day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Complaints",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.225",
      "values:originalText": "If, in relation to a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia:\n(a) a complaint is made, on or after the commencement day,\nabout the Judge; and\n(b) the circumstances that gave rise to the complaint occurred\nbefore the commencement day;\nthen:\n(c) the Chief Judge may deal with the complaint under\nsection 145 of the new law; and\n(d) for the purposes of dealing with the complaint, the reference\nto the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition of\nrelevant belief in subsection 145(4) of the new law is taken\nto include a reference to the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "If, in relation to a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia:\n(a) a complaint is made, on or after the commencement day,\nabout the Judge; and\n(b) the circumstances that gave rise to the complaint occurred\nbefore the commencement day;\nthen:\n(c) the Chief Judge may deal with the complaint under\nsection 145 of the new law; and\n(d) for the purposes of dealing with the complaint, the reference\nto the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition of\nrelevant belief in subsection 145(4) of the new law is taken\nto include a reference to the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-dialectical-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-linearlogic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f49c4e22bdd4f6c69548e625ce615447e828cc48c2e51325ff87ec5198da164d",
      "skos:note": "Chief Judge must deal with complaint about a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Complaints",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 225,
      "values:originalText": "If, in relation to a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia:\n(a) a complaint is made, on or after the commencement day,\nabout the Judge; and\n(b) the circumstances that gave rise to the complaint occurred\nbefore the commencement day;\nthen:\n(c) the Chief Judge may deal with the complaint under\nsection 145 of the new law; and\n(d) for the purposes of dealing with the complaint, the reference\nto the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition of\nrelevant belief in subsection 145(4) of the new law is taken\nto include a reference to the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Chief Judge must deal with complaint.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Complaint made about a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Chief Judge deals with complaint."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Complaint must occur before commencement day for Chief Judge to deal with it.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Complaint made on or after commencement day.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Complaint occurred before commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IMPLIES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Chief Judge's dealing with complaint implies a duty to address concerns about Judges.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Chief Judge deals with complaint.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Chief Judge addresses concerns about Judges."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-dialectical-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Dialectical"
      },
      "cml:operator": "NOT-A",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Chief Judge's dealing with complaint does not imply a duty to address all concerns about Judges.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dialectical",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Chief Judge deals with complaint.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Chief Judge does not address all concerns about Judges."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-24-logic-linearlogic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "AND",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Chief Judge's dealing with complaint and addressing concerns about Judges are related duties.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Chief Judge deals with complaint.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Chief Judge addresses concerns about Judges."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Appeals to the High Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.226",
      "values:originalText": "If:\n(a) on the day before the commencement day, an application for\nspecial leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the\nFamily Law Act 1975; and\n(b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by\nthis Act, on the commencement day the time for making the\napplication has not ended;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the application may be made\nto the High Court.",
      "skos:definition": "If:\n(a) on the day before the commencement day, an application for\nspecial leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the\nFamily Law Act 1975; and\n(b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by\nthis Act, on the commencement day the time for making the\napplication has not ended;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the application may be made\nto the High Court.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab7f1509137bdf53decf4efb62dc3541b2a1c4fd9b53a6c02528dd73c43af5f6",
      "skos:note": "Application for special leave to appeal can be made after commencement day if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Appeals to the High Court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 226,
      "values:originalText": "If:\n(a) on the day before the commencement day, an application for\nspecial leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the\nFamily Law Act 1975; and\n(b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by\nthis Act, on the commencement day the time for making the\napplication has not ended;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the application may be made\nto the High Court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "can",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application can be made",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Application for special leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the Family Law Act 1975.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Application may be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Time has passed since application could be made under section 95 of the Family Law Act 1975",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "on the day before the commencement day, an application for special leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the Family Law Act 1975;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Application may be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "and",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Two conditions must be met",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) on the day before the commencement day, an application for special leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the Family Law Act 1975; and (b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act, on the commencement day the time for making the application has not ended;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Application may be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application may be made",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If: (a) on the day before the commencement day, an application for special leave to appeal could be made under section 95 of the Family Law Act 1975; and (b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act, on the commencement day the time for making the application has not ended;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Application may be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-25-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "on or after",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application must be made on or after commencement day",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "then, on or after the commencement day, the application may be made to the High Court.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Application may be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Appeals to Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.226",
      "values:originalText": "(Division 1)\n(1)\nIf:\n(a) on the day before the commencement day, either:\n(i) an appeal could be instituted under Part X of the Family\nLaw Act 1975; or\n(ii) an application for leave to appeal could be made under\nsection 94AA of that Act; and\n(b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by\nthis Act, on the commencement day the time for instituting\nthe appeal or making the application has not ended;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the appeal or application may\nbe made to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1).\n(2)\nFor the purposes of subitem (1), an appeal or application for leave to\nappeal must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court made under\nChapter 3 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nTransitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) is to hear and determine the appeal or application\naccording to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\nand\n(b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and\n(c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(Division 1)\n(1)\nIf:\n(a) on the day before the commencement day, either:\n(i) an appeal could be instituted under Part X of the Family\nLaw Act 1975; or\n(ii) an application for leave to appeal could be made under\nsection 94AA of that Act; and\n(b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by\nthis Act, on the commencement day the time for instituting\nthe appeal or making the application has not ended;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the appeal or application may\nbe made to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1).\n(2)\nFor the purposes of subitem (1), an appeal or application for leave to\nappeal must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court made under\nChapter 3 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nTransitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) is to hear and determine the appeal or application\naccording to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\nand\n(b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and\n(c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26-logic-linearlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c0eccef941b217f24c438bffeedf1d523ed3575153aebb7886e057c9be5240d7",
      "skos:note": "Appeals can be made to Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia after commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Appeals to Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 226,
      "values:originalText": "(Division 1)\n(1)\nIf:\n(a) on the day before the commencement day, either:\n(i) an appeal could be instituted under Part X of the Family\nLaw Act 1975; or\n(ii) an application for leave to appeal could be made under\nsection 94AA of that Act; and\n(b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by\nthis Act, on the commencement day the time for instituting\nthe appeal or making the application has not ended;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the appeal or application may\nbe made to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1).\n(2)\nFor the purposes of subitem (1), an appeal or application for leave to\nappeal must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court made under\nChapter 3 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act\n2021.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nTransitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(3)\nTo avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) is to hear and determine the appeal or application\naccording to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\nand\n(b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and\n(c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant."
    },
    {
