    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27 Extensions of time to appeal or seek leave to appeal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.227",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act,\nif, on the commencement day, a person could seek an extension of time:\n(a) to institute an appeal under the Family Law Act 1975; or\n(b) to apply for leave to appeal under that Act;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the person may apply to the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) to seek such\nan extension of time.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) is to hear and determine the application according to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\nand\n(b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and\n(c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nDespite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act,\nif, on the commencement day, a person could seek an extension of time:\n(a) to institute an appeal under the Family Law Act 1975; or\n(b) to apply for leave to appeal under that Act;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the person may apply to the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) to seek such\nan extension of time.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) is to hear and determine the application according to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\nand\n(b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and\n(c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-27-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-27-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0153947dd51e7f03749d9332caa05c02c943296fb7defae0113b56ba72651cff",
      "skos:note": "Allow person to apply for extension of time after commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-27",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "27 Extensions of time to appeal or seek leave to appeal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 227,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act,\nif, on the commencement day, a person could seek an extension of time:\n(a) to institute an appeal under the Family Law Act 1975; or\n(b) to apply for leave to appeal under that Act;\nthen, on or after the commencement day, the person may apply to the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) to seek such\nan extension of time.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) is to hear and determine the application according to:\n(a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\nand\n(b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and\n(c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant."
    },
