    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-32",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32 Constituting a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and Family",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-32"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.234",
      "values:originalText": "Court of Australia (Division 1)\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(3) and 30(1), if:\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nTransitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(a) one or more of the Judges involved in hearing and\ndetermining the application, appeal or special case are not\navailable to constitute a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1); and\n(b) the allocation of another Judge is necessary to constitute a\nFull Court;\nthe Chief Justice must allocate another Judge of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1) to be a member of the Full\nCourt.\n(2)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(3) and 30(1), if:\n(a) one or more of the Judges involved in hearing and\ndetermining the application, appeal or special case are not\navailable to constitute a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1) otherwise considers it necessary;\nthe Chief Justice may allocate another Judge of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1) to be a member of the Full\nCourt.",
      "skos:definition": "Court of Australia (Division 1)\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(3) and 30(1), if:\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nTransitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(a) one or more of the Judges involved in hearing and\ndetermining the application, appeal or special case are not\navailable to constitute a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1); and\n(b) the allocation of another Judge is necessary to constitute a\nFull Court;\nthe Chief Justice must allocate another Judge of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1) to be a member of the Full\nCourt.\n(2)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(3) and 30(1), if:\n(a) one or more of the Judges involved in hearing and\ndetermining the application, appeal or special case are not\navailable to constitute a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1) otherwise considers it necessary;\nthe Chief Justice may allocate another Judge of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1) to be a member of the Full\nCourt.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-32-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-32-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "208256f1229da0d6de287bac6ca86b72a97b924ca46fe9288ace8e29dea94949",
      "skos:note": "Allocation of another Judge to constitute a Full Court"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32 Constituting a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and Family",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 234,
      "values:originalText": "Court of Australia (Division 1)\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(3) and 30(1), if:\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 5\nTransitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4\nNo. 13, 2021\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential\nAmendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021\n(a) one or more of the Judges involved in hearing and\ndetermining the application, appeal or special case are not\navailable to constitute a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1); and\n(b) the allocation of another Judge is necessary to constitute a\nFull Court;\nthe Chief Justice must allocate another Judge of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1) to be a member of the Full\nCourt.\n(2)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(3) and 30(1), if:\n(a) one or more of the Judges involved in hearing and\ndetermining the application, appeal or special case are not\navailable to constitute a Full Court of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1); and\n(b) the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 1) otherwise considers it necessary;\nthe Chief Justice may allocate another Judge of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia (Division 1) to be a member of the Full\nCourt."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-32-norm",
