    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-33",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33 Unavailability of a Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-33"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.235",
      "values:originalText": "Court of Australia (Division 1)\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(4) and 31(1), if the single Judge of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) involved in\nhearing and determining the application or appeal is not available to\ndeliver judgment in relation to the application or appeal, the Chief\nJustice must allocate another Judge of the Court to do so.\n(2)\nThe Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) so allocated:\n(a) may have regard to any evidence given or received, and\narguments adduced, by or before the Judge of the Family\nCourt of Australia before the commencement day; and\n(b) may receive further evidence or submissions, or hear further\nargument, if required.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Court of Australia (Division 1)\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(4) and 31(1), if the single Judge of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) involved in\nhearing and determining the application or appeal is not available to\ndeliver judgment in relation to the application or appeal, the Chief\nJustice must allocate another Judge of the Court to do so.\n(2)\nThe Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) so allocated:\n(a) may have regard to any evidence given or received, and\narguments adduced, by or before the Judge of the Family\nCourt of Australia before the commencement day; and\n(b) may receive further evidence or submissions, or hear further\nargument, if required.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-33-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-33-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "590e7df1556f44b7189170a08810a7b2c5b85df3c8baf14eabe676eab90577e0",
      "skos:note": "Allocate another Judge if single Judge is unavailable"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-33",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33 Unavailability of a Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 235,
      "values:originalText": "Court of Australia (Division 1)\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subitems 28(4) and 31(1), if the single Judge of the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) involved in\nhearing and determining the application or appeal is not available to\ndeliver judgment in relation to the application or appeal, the Chief\nJustice must allocate another Judge of the Court to do so.\n(2)\nThe Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 1) so allocated:\n(a) may have regard to any evidence given or received, and\narguments adduced, by or before the Judge of the Family\nCourt of Australia before the commencement day; and\n(b) may receive further evidence or submissions, or hear further\nargument, if required.\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-33-norm",
