    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 Other matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.236",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf an application is made before, on or after the commencement day that\nrelates, or is incidental, to a proceeding mentioned in a preceding item\nof this Part, then the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1) may give any direction necessary to\nensure that the application is heard and determined, and judgment is\ndelivered, pending the disposal of the proceeding.\n(2)\nWhen giving a direction, as allowed by subitem (1), the Chief Justice\nmust consider the workload and resources of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf an application is made before, on or after the commencement day that\nrelates, or is incidental, to a proceeding mentioned in a preceding item\nof this Part, then the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1) may give any direction necessary to\nensure that the application is heard and determined, and judgment is\ndelivered, pending the disposal of the proceeding.\n(2)\nWhen giving a direction, as allowed by subitem (1), the Chief Justice\nmust consider the workload and resources of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-34-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-34-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f07947bf2a07fae548e1a57401e66ba5d46d9fd221feee1580f81fd11f41259f",
      "skos:note": "Chief Justice may give direction to ensure application is heard and determined pending proceeding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 Other matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 236,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf an application is made before, on or after the commencement day that\nrelates, or is incidental, to a proceeding mentioned in a preceding item\nof this Part, then the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 1) may give any direction necessary to\nensure that the application is heard and determined, and judgment is\ndelivered, pending the disposal of the proceeding.\n(2)\nWhen giving a direction, as allowed by subitem (1), the Chief Justice\nmust consider the workload and resources of the Federal Circuit and\nFamily Court of Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-34-norm",
