    {
      "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-38",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38 Transitional rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-38"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.237",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules prescribing\nmatters of a transitional nature (including prescribing any saving or\napplication provisions) relating to:\n(a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or\n(b) the enactment of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n(b) provide powers of:\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n(c) impose a tax;\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund under an appropriation in this Act or the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules prescribing\nmatters of a transitional nature (including prescribing any saving or\napplication provisions) relating to:\n(a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or\n(b) the enactment of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n(b) provide powers of:\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n(c) impose a tax;\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund under an appropriation in this Act or the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-38-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0091eb04ddf37d5afd09a38aac1e3c1c6d0f2c9ecab90a9de78ddaab19c46e94",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may make rules prescribing transitional matters."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2021a00013rec01#sch-5-sec-38",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "38 Transitional rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 237,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules prescribing\nmatters of a transitional nature (including prescribing any saving or\napplication provisions) relating to:\n(a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or\n(b) the enactment of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia Act 2021.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n(b) provide powers of:\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n(c) impose a tax;\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund under an appropriation in this Act or the\nFederal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021;\n\nSchedule 5  Transitional provisions"
    },
